                "r": 327.88345000000015,
                "b": 630.8444836198181,
                "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"
              },
              "charspan": [
                0,
                332
              ]
            }
          ],
          "orig": "Warhammer 40,000 battlefields are strewn with a wide variety of obstacles, structures and detritus collectively known as terrain features (see pages 44-48). When a model makes any kind of move, it can be moved over a terrain feature but not through it (so models can't move through a wall, for example, but can climb up or over it).",
          "text": "Warhammer 40,000 battlefields are strewn with a wide variety of obstacles, structures and detritus collectively known as terrain features (see pages 44-48). When a model makes any kind of move, it can be moved over a terrain feature but not through it (so models can't move through a wall, for example, but can climb up or over it)."
        },
        {
          "self_ref": "#/texts/343",
          "parent": {
            "$ref": "#/body"
          },
          "children": [],
          "content_layer": "body",
          "label": "text",
          "prov": [
            {
              "page_no": 15,
              "bbox": {
                "l": 162.0748,
                "t": 618.3917000000001,
                "r": 326.11545,
                "b": 530.8759836198183,
                "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"
              },
              "charspan": [
                0,
                399
              ]
            }
          ],
          "orig": "A model can be moved over terrain features that are 2\" or less in height as if they were not there. A model can be moved vertically in order to climb up or down any terrain features that are taller than this, counting the vertical distance up and/or down as part of its move. Models cannot end any kind of move mid-climb - if it is not possible to end the move as a result, that move cannot be made.",
          "text": "A model can be moved over terrain features that are 2\" or less in height as if they were not there. A model can be moved vertically in order to climb up or down any terrain features that are taller than this, counting the vertical distance up and/or down as part of its move. Models cannot end any kind of move mid-climb - if it is not possible to end the move as a result, that move cannot be made."
        },
